# Fixed one-line dungeon descriptions, picked by the seed (not random).
[dungeon.flavor.net]
A router cave of humming relays.
Tunnels of beacons and lost packets.
A mesh of halls that hop channels.
An access point with a deep basement.
Halls lined with blinking antennas.
A maze of handshakes and timeouts.
A relay tower, upside down.
A packet storm in a stone shell.
A cave where every echo is a ping.
Long corridors of crowded channels.
A router with too many hallways.
Wide halls full of drifting frames.
An uplink that leads only down.
A signal forest of copper roots.
A busy hub that never sleeps.
A beacon shrine buried in noise.
A labyrinth of SSIDs and spam.
A tunnel net spun by worms.
Stacked floors of lagging traffic.
A gateway to a deeper gateway.

[dungeon.flavor.volt]
A coil maze that buzzes in the dark.
A battery vault with sparking floors.
Twisty halls that want to pair.
A speaker crypt full of static.
A charged cave of tiny devices.
Copper tunnels with live wires.
A pairing chamber with no exit.
Halls that pulse at 2.4 GHz.
A storm in a matchbox.
A gadget graveyard, still humming.
Narrow corridors of short range.
A low-energy cave with high voltage.
A headset hive, buzzing softly.
A lab of loose wires and sparks.
A tower of tangled earbuds.
Static rooms that raise your fur.
A smartwatch tomb, still ticking.
A buzzing hive of beacons.
A cave lit only by sparks.
An arc of halls that crackle.

